            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I used fat free vanilla yogurt and skim milk to keep it on the lighter side. This was very good for breakfast."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Idahed"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe got me started on smoothies. Given what ingredients I had, I substituted 2 Tbs of honey for the sugar and 1/2 cup of lemonade for the pineapple and orange juice. Turned out great. I also had some granola which I threw into the glass, on top of the smoothie. It added a nice crunch! Thanks for the recipe!!!",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-22T02:28:38.400Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Julie Perrin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this with a few changes. I added about 1/8 cup OJ of and same of almond milk. I did not have pineapple juice. I did not add sugar. I added about 2tbs of plain yogurt, 5 spinach leaves and used Wyman's frozen mixed berries. This is yummy and I think the OJ adds a nice zip to the flavor. Overall healthy and yummy!",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-23T14:17:53.687Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marilyn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great base recipe. I used frozen berry mix and banana and came out great. Also chose nonfat Greek yogurt for more protein. My millennial daughter doesn’t like milk/orange/pineapple, so I substituted a zero calorie vitamin water for my “liquids”. Fit her restrictions, lessened my digestive sensitivity and lowered the calorie count. Win, win, win &amp; absolutely delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-30T13:33:45.803Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mickeymc"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe! I used strawberry kiwi juice instead of the pineapple juice and used more milk and strawberries than it called for. Absolutely delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2021-06-10T01:39:32.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
