            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "StrongUdon7350"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love it ♡ I didn't use all of the ingredients listed but I used; 1 cup banana, 1 cup strawberries, about 1 cup Chobani Vanilla Greek Yogurt, 4 tablespoons OJ &amp; I put tasteless Collage Peptides in mine too. I will use this recipe again, it's ezpzbrze to remember &amp; very yummy 😋",
            "datePublished": "2023-02-14T18:33:51.833Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sabrina"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Pretty good taste and job....being my 1st time but used FRESH cut pineapples instead of juice, almond milk, blueberries, light Greek yogurt, ice cubes, and about 1/4 of a banana. No sugar or orange juice. Children like it.",
            "datePublished": "2019-06-10T14:49:55.410Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shauna Capps"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I appreciate reading other people's experience using a recipe, so here's mine. I had to use ingredients on hand, and I omitted the sugar because I've never thought a smoothie needed added sugar. I gave it a high rating because the ratio of ingredient types worked well. I used plain unsweetened Greek yogurt, apple cider instead of the pineapple juice, frozen strawberries, and since I increased the recipe by 50% I used one fresh banana plus a handful of frozen banana. No changes to other ingredients. Using frozen fruit makes it thicker, but it was still smooth, and drinkable (no spoon required). Good enough to add to my recipe box. Without the pineapple juice, I felt it should be labeled Strawberry Banana Yogurt Smoothie.",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-30T21:44:11.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "seattlemama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was great without OJ or milk or sugar but pineapple juice is essential. Trying different smoothies since my 12yr old just got braces and he approved! I tried it I too and it was good. I did use vanilla yogurt that had sugar it which is why I didn’t add sugar.",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-15T02:58:41.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
